First Author: Koziński
Title: Harnessing deep learning to detect bronchiolitis obliterans syndrome from chest CT
Source number: 26  ￼

Very short summary: This study developed a deep neural network to detect bronchiolitis obliterans syndrome (BOS) from chest CT scans after lung transplantation. Five key findings were: (1) the analysis included 75 post-transplant patients, 26 with BOS and 49 without BOS; (2) the model achieved an aggregated ROC-AUC of 0.90 (95% CI 0.840–0.953) for BOS detection; (3) performance increased with BOS severity, with ROC-AUC 0.88 for stage I, 0.91 for stage II, and 0.94 for stage III; (4) the model also identified at-risk patients with FEV1 80–90% of best FEV1 with ROC-AUC 0.87 (95% CI 0.735–0.974); and (5) the DNN performed comparably on standard- and high-resolution CT and highlighted hyperlucent/hypoattenuated regions suggestive of air-trapping or bronchiectasis. Tables 1–2 and Figures 1–4 were directly used for this extraction.  ￼

