	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: The study excluded scans with large pixel size, too few slices, and scans of patients with extensive infiltrates, which is most consistent with complete-case/exclusion-based handling rather than imputation. Class imbalance was addressed in the design and evaluation by patient-level five-fold splitting and weighted ROC analysis to avoid bias from patients with more scans, but no oversampling was described. Data preprocessing and acquisition details were described in depth, including scan inclusion/exclusion, reconstruction type, and late-fusion slice handling. Because the study used five-fold cross-validation at the patient level, fixed training/test N were not reported. Code availability was not reported in the retrieved text.  ￼

